jobs.description:
Vacaturebeschrijving
   Join a leading logistics organization with a modern fleet featuring top brands like Volvo and DAF. To support the expansion of our operations, we are looking for driven CE Truck Drivers to elevate our hooklift container transport. You will be on the road from Monday to Friday and enjoy your well-deserved rest over the weekend.  Functieomschrijving:
 What you will do as a CE Truck Driver- Transport hooklift containers throughout the Netherlands and occasionally Germany in a modern Volvo or DAF;
- Work on the road from Monday to Friday, sleeping in your own dedicated cab;
- Work 60 to 70 hours per week and enjoy 2 full weeks off every 8 weeks;
- Safely deliver and drop off containers at various client sites and locations;
- Accurately maintain journey logs and keep your truck in top condition.


  Functievereisten:
 What you bring as a CE Truck Driver- A valid CE driver's license, Code 95, and driver card;
- Willingness to spend nights in the cab from Monday to Friday;
- Own transportation to travel to the depot;
- A flexible mindset to work 60 to 70 hours per week;
- Good command of either the Dutch or English language.


  Arbeidsvoorwaarden:
 What you earn as a CE Truck Driver- Highly attractive gross monthly salary ranging from €5,108.55 to €5,965.00 per month.
- Unique work schedule with 2 mandatory weeks off every 8 weeks.
- International allowance and an average net allowance of €200 per week for travel and accommodation costs.
- Access to your own dedicated truck right after the onboarding period.
- Fully covered hotel accommodation during the onboarding period.
- Guaranteed weekends off, every single week.
- Drive modern, new equipment (DAF and Volvo) from a continuously renewed fleet.
- An international and accessible work environment where English-speaking drivers are warmly welcomed.

Ready to sink your teeth into the role of CE Truck Driver in the Amsterdam area? Apply now—it takes just 2 minutes! 
Salarisomschrijving€

Wat je gaat doen As a production worker in the cheese factory, you work in the shaving department. Here, large cheese blocks are prepared for the next stage of production.

Your tasks include:- placing 15 kg cheese blocks at your workstation;
- using a machine to remove the outer layer of the cheese;
- checking that the cheese is processed correctly;
- moving processed cheese with an electric pallet truck;
- keeping your workstation clean, safe and organised;
- working with your team to achieve the daily production targets.

Do you not yet have experience with an EPT? That is not a problem. You can learn this on the job and may have the opportunity to obtain your EPT certificate.   Wat we je bieden Your work as a production worker is rewarded with:
- a base salary of €18,16 gross per hour;
- a 30% allowance between 18:00 and 22:00;
- a 40% allowance between 22:00 and 07:00;
- a performance bonus of up to €2.00 gross per hour;
- a full-time job in a stable 3-shift schedule;
- free weekends;
- 8% holiday pay;
- 20 vacation days and 4 additional days in a flex budget;
- travel allowance from 10 km;
- the prospect of a permanent contract;
- on-the-job training and the opportunity to obtain an EPT certificate;
- personal support from Start People at the production location.

At Start People, we operate on the principle of equal pay; your terms and conditions of employment always match those of colleagues who are employed directly by the client. This means that, in addition to your hourly rate, your terms and conditions of employment also include, for example, the number of days off, allowances, time-off-in-lieu payments and other pay components.
   Functie-eisen This job is a good match if you:- can repeatedly lift cheese blocks weighing 15 kg;
- are comfortable with standing and physical work;
- are available full-time for morning, afternoon and night shifts;
- speak and understand Dutch or English;
- have your own reliable transport;
- already have your own accom
